  "mach:foundation": "openEHR Foundation (non-profit, est. 2003)",
  "mach:category": "interoperability-standards",
  "mach:subcategory": "openehr",
  "mach:maturity": "production",
  "mach:judgement": "Adopt",
  "mach:judgementReason": "Mature, foundation-governed standard deployed nationally in Norway, Australia, Brazil, Slovenia, and many others since the early 2000s. Its two-level modelling approach — separating stable technical specs from clinician-defined archetypes — is uniquely suited to semantically rich, long-lived EHR data. Multiple open-source implementations exist (EHRbase, EtherCIS, Atomik). Active specification programme with regular releases. Strongly complementary to FHIR; the two standards increasingly converge via FHIR profiles over openEHR archetypes.",
  "mach:editorialReviewedAt": "2026-05-01",
